        "original_id": "ff06f69d-3b2b-5041-92ff-6732f320c1ee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Dr. Ronald E. McNair Academic High School, NASA\n- People: Ronald Erwin McNair, Cheryl McNair\n- Places: Jersey City, Hudson County, New Jersey, United States\n- Topics: Challenger disaster\n\nFacts:\n- Ronald Erwin McNair was born on October 21, 1950, and he was an American physicist and NASA astronaut.\n- Ronald Erwin McNair died on January 28, 1986, in the Space Shuttle Challenger disaster.\n- Ronald Erwin McNair was survived by his wife, Cheryl, and two children.\n- Dr. Ronald E. McNair Academic High School is a magnet public high school at 123 Coles Street in Jersey City, Hudson County, New Jersey, United States.\n- Dr. Ronald E. McNair Academic High School was often called Academic before its dedication and is also known as McNair.\n- Dr. Ronald E. McNair Academic High School is named in memory of Ronald Erwin McNair.",
